---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import AuthorBio from "../components/AuthorBio.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About — ${siteConfig.name}`}
  description={`About ${siteConfig.name}: a single-author technical blog covering Dev Tools, Data & Automation, AI Productivity, and Guides & Fixes.`}
  noindex
>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      {siteConfig.name} is a single-author technical blog built around one rule: every
      post exists to solve one real, specific problem, not to fill a content calendar.
      If you landed here searching an exact error message, a specific CLI flag, or
      how one tool actually behaves compared to another in practice, that's the kind
      of question this site is written to answer.
    </p>

    <p>Four areas get covered, each for a different kind of question:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Dev Tools</strong> — editors, CLIs, Git workflows, and the tooling
        developers reach for every day.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Data &amp; Automation</strong> — CI/CD, deploy pipelines, and scripts
        that remove a manual step from someone's week.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>AI Productivity</strong> — using AI coding assistants well: prompting,
        review habits, and where they genuinely help versus where they don't.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Guides &amp; Fixes</strong> — the specific bug, the specific error,
        the fix that isn't in the official docs yet.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <AuthorBio />

    <p>
      Every post is fact-checked and run by the author before it's published —
      see the <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> for exactly how. Spotted
      something outdated, or have a topic worth covering? <a href="/contact/"
        >Get in touch</a
      >.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
